# Implementation Plan

## Scenario 1 - Room Setup & Lobby (Complete)

## Scenario 4 - Result, Restart & Final Validation

### Discovery Notes
- **Gaps identified:**
  - `RoomStatus` needs `result`.
  - No endpoints for `POST /rooms/:code/end` or `POST /rooms/:code/restart`.
  - `ResultPanel` and `GamePage` need to handle the `result` status.
- **Assumptions:**
  - `scores` should be reset on restart as well, or should they persist? The spec says "all round state cleared", so I'll reset scores.

### State Model Changes
#### Backend
- `backend/src/models/game.ts`:
  - `RoomStatus`: Add `result`.

### Data Flow
- **End Round**: `POST /rooms/:code/end` (Host only) -> Sets status to `result`.
- **Restart**: `POST /rooms/:code/restart` (Host only) -> Resets status to `lobby` and clears round data.
- **Sync**: Polling players redirect to lobby on `status === 'lobby'` from `result`.

### File-level Changes
- `backend/src/models/game.ts`: Update status enum.
- `backend/src/services/roomStore.ts`: Add `endRound` and `restartGame`.
- `backend/src/api/rooms.ts`: Add end and restart routes.
- `frontend/src/state/roomStore.ts`: Add `endRound` and `restartGame`.
- `frontend/src/pages/GamePage.tsx`: Conditional rendering for `result` state.
- `frontend/src/components/ResultPanel.tsx`: Display final results.

### Risks
- Ensuring all players see the result screen before the host restarts.
